    },
    {
      "text": "Add the olive oil and once it’s hot add in the collard greens, onion, jalapeno, green bell pepper, and garlic. Cook this down until soft then add in the paprika, red pepper flakes, salt, and pepper.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-southern-shakshuka/#wprm-recipe-53195-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/keto-southern-goat-cheese-shaksuka-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir in the crushed tomatoes then continue cooking until the sauce is nice and hot. Turn off the heat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-southern-shakshuka/#wprm-recipe-53195-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/keto-southern-goat-cheese-shaksuka-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use a spoon to create wells in the sauce, then crack an egg into each.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-southern-shakshuka/#wprm-recipe-53195-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/keto-southern-goat-cheese-shaksuka-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the skillet into the oven and bake for 5 minutes or so, until the egg whites are set.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-southern-shakshuka/#wprm-recipe-53195-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/keto-southern-goat-cheese-shaksuka-05.jpg"
    },
